When the UE is registered with a PLMN over a non‑3GPP access, both the AMF and the UE maintain:

a) the registration state and state machine for non‑3GPP access;

b) the 5G NAS security context;

c) the registration area for non‑3GPP access (which is associated with a single TAI); and

d) the non‑3GPP de‑registration timer (maintained by the UE) and the corresponding non‑3GPP implicit de‑registration timer (maintained by the AMF).
